{"schema_version":1,"architecture_version":3,"workstream_id":"AAYS_21_SLOT_SAFE_PARALLEL_V1","slot_id":"height_difference_3","task_id":"height_difference_3-canonical-api-measurement-20260721-01","continuation_key":"6e8e709b6bad7b9807055e2b8b5de98cd4945ee3dee57825e72ba1b824eadd0f","created_at":"2026-08-01T07:58:00Z","claim_commit_sha":"74bbc4551fdd68e251f3e161cdae3cf7aac47d52","state":"RASTER_SPACE_AFFINE_PIXEL_CENTER_RESAMPLING_AND_SUPPORT_SCALE_GATE_QUALIFIED_RUNTIME_HELD","purpose":"Qualify exact raster-space semantics and reproducible same-point support evidence for EA 1m DTM and OS Terrain 50 50m cross-checks without executing blocked runtime or promoting numeric values.","official_controls":[{"id":"OGC_GEOTIFF_RASTER_SPACE_SEMANTICS","sources":["https://docs.ogc.org/is/19-008r4/19-008r4.html"],"facts":["GTRasterTypeGeoKey distinguishes PixelIsArea and PixelIsPoint","PixelIsArea references the upper-left pixel corner while PixelIsPoint references a point pixel at its center","accurate georeferencing requires the raster-space type and raster-to-model transformation"],"decision":"Require GTRasterTypeGeoKey/AREA_OR_POINT, ModelTiepoint/ModelPixelScale or transformation metadata and explicit pixel-center convention for every EA GeoTIFF."},{"id":"GDAL_RFC33_HALF_PIXEL_AND_AREA_OR_POINT","sources":["https://gdal.org/en/stable/development/rfc/rfc33_gtiff_pixelispoint.html","https://gdal.org/en/stable/drivers/raster/gtiff.html"],"facts":["GDAL applies a half-pixel correction for PixelIsPoint when forming the geotransform","AREA_OR_POINT metadata is stored through RasterPixelIsPoint","legacy ignore behavior can change apparent georeferencing"],"decision":"Record AREA_OR_POINT and GTIFF_POINT_GEO_IGNORE state; reject ambiguous or legacy half-pixel behavior."},{"id":"GDAL_AFFINE_PIXEL_CENTER_AND_INDEX_TRACE","sources":["https://gdal.org/en/stable/tutorials/geotransforms_tut.html","https://gdal.org/en/stable/programs/gdal_raster_pixel_info.html"],"facts":["the six-term geotransform maps pixel/line coordinates to georeferenced coordinates","the center of the top-left pixel is at pixel/line 0.5,0.5","pixel queries can report the converted column,line and value"],"decision":"Persist the full affine transform, selected row/column, pixel-center easting/northing, query coordinate and center offset for both sources."},{"id":"GDAL_RESAMPLING_NODATA_AND_REPRODUCIBILITY","sources":["https://gdal.org/en/stable/programs/gdalwarp.html","https://gdal.org/en/stable/doxygen/structGDALWarpOptions.html"],"facts":["nearest, bilinear, average and other kernels have different support and weighting semantics","nodata/masks change which source pixels contribute","chunk-dependent XSCALE/YSCALE and approximate transformation can affect output reproducibility"],"decision":"Record whether any warp/resample occurred, algorithm, source/target resolution, nodata policy, overview use, XSCALE/YSCALE and error threshold; no hidden resampling."},{"id":"EA1M_TERRAIN50_50M_SUPPORT_SCALE_CONTRACT","sources":["https://environment.data.gov.uk/dataset/13787b9a-26a4-4775-8523-806d13af58fc","https://docs.os.uk/os-downloads/products/land-and-terrain-portfolio/os-terrain-50/os-terrain-50-technical-specification/grid-data","https://rasterio.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/rasterio.vrt.html"],"facts":["EA Composite DTM has 1m spatial resolution","OS Terrain 50 values are calculated at centers of 50m by 50m pixels","Rasterio dataset.sample returns the nearest pixel value and does not interpolate"],"decision":"Treat the EA and OS samples as different spatial supports. Record support areas, resolution ratio, nearest-pixel selection and distance to each selected pixel center; Terrain 50 remains a coarse cross-check, not a co-located 1m observation."}],"repository_contract_control":{"id":"AAYS_NEAREST_SAMPLE_WITHOUT_GRID_SUPPORT_MANIFEST_GAP","source_path":"docs/chatgpt_status/topography/shards/height_difference_3/automation/009_sample_ea_dtm_and_os_terrain50.py","source_blob_sha":"42ac8